        "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. Independently: q-149570 has means 36 and 4, giving population covariance (0-2+4-12)/4=-2.5; q-149617 gives (0+4+4+0)/4=2. For q-278288, OV=r+(6/11)(s-r)=(5/11)r+(6/11)s. q-87564 gives variance 201/7-(35/7)^2=26/7. For q-5772, the source specifies a fair die numbered 1 through 10, whose mean is 5.5. q-127373 has mean (4+31)/2=17.5; its worked solution contains the authored typo 31·f(10), which should be 31·f(31), but its final answer is correct because both probabilities equal 1/10. q-42728 gives weighted mean 90/24=15/4. q-83642 gives (20+44+48)/10=11.2. q-127770 gives expected prize 0.4+0.6+0.6+0.4=2 dollars; the source treats prizes as profit, assuming no additional playing cost. q-123278 gives magnitude sqrt(7+9)=4. Using the listed discrete supports, q-83623 gives 0.8-0.1=0.7, q-124953 gives 1-5/8=3/8, and q-83921 gives 1-1/8=7/8; the inclusive lower endpoints require subtracting the preceding support value's CDF. The normal-table answers are q-131387: 0.9778, q-94098: 0.7734, and q-131399: 1-0.0158=0.9842. These are table-rounded probabilities, and continuity makes strict versus inclusive normal endpoints equivalent. No earlier submitted answers or grades were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
