        "knowledge_point_id": "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function",
        "problem": "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t+1},\\,t-3⟩,$ $|r(6)|=$",
        "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(6) & =⟨\\sqrt{6+1},\\,6-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{7},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(6)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{7})}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7+9} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
